WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.058 --> 00:00:01.649
You send an important message.

2
00:00:01.823 --> 00:00:03.019
It never arrives.

3
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.211
TeamChat is a messaging app for people and
teams.

4
00:00:06.594 --> 00:00:08.603
HarborCloud is its cloud platform.

5
00:00:08.986 --> 00:00:11.157
Fixing the failure needs both teams.

6
00:00:11.598 --> 00:00:15.731
But their logs can contain customer
information and private system details.

7
00:00:16.242 --> 00:00:21.025
Engineers must pick out what is safe to
share, pass findings back and forth, and

8
00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:24.009
check whether each fix actually restored
delivery.

9
00:00:24.613 --> 00:00:26.598
Relay connects their agents through Switch.

10
00:00:26.923 --> 00:00:29.024
Each investigates its own systems.

11
00:00:29.628 --> 00:00:32.449
Only owner-approved findings reach the
other team.

12
00:00:33.053 --> 00:00:36.060
Each company approves changes to its own
systems.

13
00:00:36.664 --> 00:00:41.273
Then both teams test what customers care
about: did the messages arrive?

14
00:00:41.877 --> 00:00:46.613
Here's how. Maya reports the problem in the
shared Mattermost incident channel.

15
00:00:47.054 --> 00:00:50.421
Leo, HarborCloud's engineer, confirms his
team is available.

16
00:00:51.025 --> 00:00:53.394
TeamChat's agent checks its own service.

17
00:00:53.835 --> 00:00:57.341
It finds connection failures and message
servers that failed to start.

18
00:00:57.945 --> 00:01:01.927
Its detailed diagnostic observations stay
in TeamChat's context.

19
00:01:02.531 --> 00:01:05.851
The agent prepares a short incident finding
and a focused question for

20
00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:10.832
HarborCloud. Maya reviews that finding,
including the highlighted question, and

21
00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.607
replies, "Share with HarborCloud."

22
00:01:14.048 --> 00:01:18.251
The exact approved text arrives in the
shared incident thread through Switch.

23
00:01:18.855 --> 00:01:22.338
HarborCloud's agent receives it and
investigates its own connection.

24
00:01:23.034 --> 00:01:25.937
It finds the overload and proposes more
capacity.

25
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:31.754
Leo reviews the change in his private
workroom and replies, "Approve this
change."

26
00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.250
HarborCloud's connection is healthy.

27
00:01:34.529 --> 00:01:36.955
But customers' messages are still failing.

28
00:01:37.768 --> 00:01:41.599
Relay carries that result back to
TeamChat's agent, which investigates what

29
00:01:41.645 --> 00:01:46.429
remains. It proposes recovering the failed
parts of TeamChat's message service.

30
00:01:47.032 --> 00:01:49.482
Maya reviews and approves the change.

31
00:01:49.923 --> 00:01:52.059
The agent performs the recovery.

32
00:01:52.663 --> 00:01:55.345
Its reviewed result returns to the incident
thread.

33
00:01:55.949 --> 00:02:02.114
Run the same delivery test again: 24
messages sent, 24 arrived.

34
00:02:02.892 --> 00:02:07.164
Maya asks the agent to retry an earlier
message that genuinely failed.

35
00:02:07.744 --> 00:02:09.451
The same message arrives.

36
00:02:10.032 --> 00:02:13.108
A repeated request does not create a second
copy.

37
00:02:13.782 --> 00:02:16.614
Both teams controlled what was shared and
changed.

38
00:02:17.288 --> 00:02:22.826
The incident thread records their findings,
approvals, and results: 24 messages

39
00:02:22.895 --> 00:02:26.053
delivered, and the earlier failed message
recovered.

40
00:02:26.866 --> 00:02:29.025
Relay. Two teams.

41
00:02:29.536 --> 00:02:30.558
One recovery.
